machine gun kelly on fire casey neistat  acting  oh good god and whatever the hell this  is who is that  no idea  project power is netflix's latest  superhero inspired action flick that  asks the question  what if drugs could give you superpowers  we have a crackhead lifting up the box  in this video we'll be taking a deep  dive into project power's ending  pointing out its hidden easter eggs and  how it sets itself  up for a potential sequel so pop a pill  and make sure to like and subscribe  because here  we go project power begins where it ends  at the docks in new orleans next to a  ship called  genesis it's a bit on the nose that the  ship where a new more  powerful evolution of human will be  created is named after the first book in  the bible that recounts the creation of  humanity  genesis means the origin or beginning so  it makes sense it happens  right at the beginning of the film you  can kind of make up the name of the  company responsible for this pill here  telios which comes from the greek word  for perfection  an apt name for a company that wants to  essentially create the next evolution of  humanity  our goal is simple the next evolution of  the human species  so telios begins the process of testing  the drug out by  handing it out to local drug dealers  like newt here and these drugs are  insanely powerful allowing the user to  unlock parts of their dna  giving them superpowers for 5 minutes  the drug has  different effects for each user some can  turn into fire like newt  steel skin like frank and the ability to  grow your nails like meg  the pill can also have negative effects  like some poor bastards who just explode  that's why the drug is under  quote-unquote clinical trials we learn  from this guy here known as biggie for  reasons that will become apparent that  telios wants to harness the power and  make it  permanent imagine the power you could  wield if you had an army  of super-powered soldiers that's why he  brings a group of rich investors to  witness this power firsthand but before  we get there we're introduced to robin  reilly a high schooler pushing the power  pill to pay for her mother's surgery and  medical needs  she's actually working alongside new  orleans police officer  frank played by joseph gordon-levitt to  keep the drug off the streets  it's kind of a mutually beneficial  relationship she gets paid and he makes  sure one less pill is out of the hands  of criminals he's seen how one person on  the drug can take down an entire  precinct  and he wants to get the bottom of who's  behind it frank is the stereotypical  good  bad cop even doing impressions of clint  eastwood the actor whose many rules  portrayed that trope  he pays off dealers but for the right  reasons even giving up his bike to robin  he uses the drug too  but only to take down others who use it  on the other end of the spectrum  is art portrayed by jamie foxx like  frank he wants to bring down the  organization that is creating these  pills but  unlike frank he's not motivated by a  noble sense of making the city a safer  place  he wants one thing and one thing only  the safe return of his daughter and  he'll do anything to get that  even if it means kidnapping a high  schooler he does bad things but for good  reasons  so frank and art are quite similar  they're just motivated in different ways  art tracks down newt and i love this  subtle line as he answers the door  you alone are we all we haven't really  met art yet nor do we know about his  daughter but this line sets up his  motivation his loneliness brought upon  by the loss of his daughter  art wants to know who newt's supplier is  but newt pops a couple pills in order to  fight him off his power is turning into  flames which ironically is also what  happens when  eminem drops a diss track on him  while newt spontaneously combusts after  od on the pill we get our first glimpse  of art's daughter via flashback as we'll  learn throughout the film  art's daughter was taken from him by  telios she is the first human to have an  ability that  doesn't require the pill making her a  priceless lab rat for tellios to  experiment on  you see years ago art was a ranger for  the us military and telios being a  defense contractor  took a group of these rangers and  performed experiments on them  try to turn us into superheroes in brief  flashbacks we see that art's power was  unlocked by telios but he managed to  escape  eventually having a daughter named tracy  and it seems as though the ability to  unlock one's superpower was passed on to  his daughter kinda like fetal alcohol  syndrome yes that weird scene  where the teacher talks about how taking  drugs during pregnancy can have adverse  effects on children applies to the power  drug as well  tracy has somehow inherited power  through her father  but we'll get to that in a bit by using  newt's phone to schedule a meeting art  tracks down ramen and kidnaps her hoping  to get a lead on this mysterious bearded  man  the man who stole his daughter they make  their way to an asian supermarket and  learn that not only is telios  distributing the drug  but they're also tracking its users you  can even make out youtuber casey neistat  here another interesting thing to note  is that the office is actually located  on the back of a truck  making it a mobile unit this allows them  to go about undetected  heck even their main research facility  is located on a boat where they can move  from port to port although art and  robin's relationship gets off to a rocky  start when he kidnaps her  they soon form a bond ramen has lost a  father and art has lost his daughter  there's even a scene where he mistakes  her for his girl  this love for his daughter and children  in general is shown in a quick scene at  the gas station where he tries to make  this little girl smile  these small moments show us his humanity  a humanity rooted in the love for his  daughter  ramen ends up helping him for cash cash  covered in blood  literal blood money and as she makes the  decision whether or not to help him a  soup can rolls by her foot  she was supposed to pick up suit for her  mother reminding her of the things we do  for family  and with art telling her he's doing this  for his daughter she eventually ends up  helping him out  taking him to the vet clinic where her  mom works to stitch him up there's some  kind of irony here that as he's being  patched up there are caged animals in  the background just like he used to be  caged up by telios and how his own  daughter is  as well but there's a deeper discussion  that takes place between art and robin  that gets to the social commentary the  film is trying to explore  it's that the system is designed to keep  the people in power  in power and the people not in power  down  because in the real world the power goes  to where it always goes to the people  that already have it robin is the  perfect example of how the system makes  it difficult for her to do  anything but sell drugs her mother is a  hard-working vet tech but still can't  afford to pay for medical bills or  surgery robin can't get a job past  minimum wage so the easiest option for  her to make fast cash is selling drugs  art tells her that the way out of the  system is to find what you're good at  something we see at the end of the film  when one of her rap songs makes it on  the radio  and we see her by the pier writing  lyrics meanwhile frank is after art  after being told by the chief that art  is the one behind pushing these drugs  as we'll find out chief crane is part of  this whole conspiracy  he's working with telios to bring down  art who could jeopardize their entire  plan  i also want to mention that throughout  much of the film frank wears a new  orleans saints jersey he's the good guy  so saints is an appropriate jersey but  it's the name on the back which is more  interesting  number 37 steve gleason steve was a  safety for the saints from 2006 to 2007  where he's best known for one of the  most memorable blocks in football  history a block which led to the saints  first  point in 21 months after the superdome  was closed due to hurricane katrina  in 2011 gleason revealed he was battling  als  and became an advocate for als awareness  eventually being awarded the  congressional gold medal for his  contributions so it's kind of fitting  the heroic character in this story wears  the jersey of a heroic character  in real life frank ends up joining  forces with art after he finds out the  truth that art's daughter was captured  so that the pill could be synthesized  and tested on the new orleans populace  once it gets mass produced however the  problem will spread all across the world  if they can stabilize it then they'll  mass produce it  so whatever's happening here it's gonna  start happening everywhere  art turns himself into telios as a part  of a greater plan to save his daughter  there we meet head scientist gardner and  learn her justification for unleashing  dangerous drugs and performing  experiments on children she believes  she's a pioneer ushering in humanity to  its next  logical evolution she brings up the  example of henrietta lacks a woman whose  cancer cells were studied because  unlike normal people cells that died  when exposed to cancer  hers doubled the experiments done to her  helped scientists better understand how  viruses work  the effect of radiation on the body and  ultimately played a large role in the  development of the polio vaccine perhaps  it's a coincidence but both henrietta  and tracy are women of color  gardner believes the ends justify the  means that it's okay to do  a little bad for the greater good which  seems to be a recurring theme throughout  this film before art is saved by frank  he hints at his powers by comparing it  to that of a pistol shrimp a pistol  shrimp can fire bullets of bubbles at  its foes so strong and fast that the  sound is louder than an actual gunshot  this makes them pound for pound one of  the strongest animals on the planet  as we'll see in the film's climax art  can fire off tremendous bursts of energy  incinerating those around him he's the  pistol shrimp of new orleans but this  energy takes its toll  essentially killing him in the process  luckily his daughter has the ability to  heal this is hinted at earlier when we  see how a plant grows as she nears it as  well as biggie's presentation to the  investors where he talks about  how some animals have the ability to  heal themselves fun fact the name tracy  is derived from native irish meaning  fighter and superior  as the characters come out victorious  art says his story is done  he has his daughter and he can live his  life there's also a great shot of his  daughter taking off her medical bracelet  symbolic of her newfound freedom frank  however hints at the bigger conspiracy  that the government will likely not stop  here  they need to be exposed potentially  opening the doors for a sequel  and robin comes home and gives her  mother the much-needed money for her  surgery  oh and that can of soup which is a fun  nod to earlier in the film  robin's music is also heard on the radio  leading us to believe she's put her life  of selling drugs behind her  and has taken art's advice to follow  what she's good at but what superhero  power do you think you'd unlock if you  took the pill  me the ability to know if a movie is  good before i watch it that's all for  this video today please make sure to  like and subscribe and for more bad  takes you can follow me on twitter at  thinkstoryyt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much
 

